From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:18:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: host GridCraft in an Intuition window through egui-aros

apps/gridcraft-aros is the desktop app's counterpart on AROS: SheetApp runs in one Intuition window through egui-aros (winit and egui-winit for the window and input, the CPU renderer or OpenGL chosen at run time with --gui-renderer or the GUI_RENDERER ToolType, ASL requesters, the system clipboard's text and pictures, OpenURL for links). Start-up data (Workbench arguments, ToolTypes, the program's drawer, absolute document names) comes from egui-aros too; this crate has no unsafe code.

Settings and the log live in GridCraftData in the program's drawer. The program runs in the -nix path mode and converts names at the requesters; recent files kept by the 0.8.0 AROS release as DOS names are converted when the settings are read. The loop has no idle poll. Not here: the control server, printing, HTML on the clipboard, the self-updater and a native window per workbook window. --screenshot, --test-steps and GRIDCRAFT_TRACE_INPUT are test aids.
